  "body": "Follow-up of #3843 / PR #3858, from the Opus safety review on PR #3858 (head `215d44a52`).\n\nThe law of #3843 (a 2D Offset whose \"Pass starts at\" is Inside or Outside takes the Arc entry unless the user selects another type) reads only the values before and after an edit; it does not see what the request named. Two doors miss it:\n\n1. **The create door does not get the law.** `crates/app/src/mcp/edit.rs:308-311`: `add_operation` patches the seed and calls `CreateOperation` directly. Probe: `add_operation {\"kind\":\"2D Offset\",\"params\":{\"pass_start\":\"outside\"}}` gives `pass_start: outside`, `entry: helix` - the bug of #3843 at another door.\n2. **An explicit Helix in the same request is replaced with Arc.** `crates/app/src/mcp/edit.rs:323-324`: `edit_operation` merges the patch onto the current params, so the law cannot see a named entry. Probe on a new 2D Offset: `edit_operation {\"params\":{\"pass_start\":\"inside\",\"entry\":\"helix\"}}` gives `entry: arc` - the user's named choice is overridden. A GUI page that sends the start side and the entry in one edit would have the same problem (only the MCP door was probed).\n\nOne rule closes the class: the door tells the law whether the request named an entry, and the create door applies the same law against the seed.\n\nDone means: both probes above give the expected entry (Arc for 1, Helix for 2), each pinned by an MCP test in `crates/app/tests/offset_pass_start/start_side_entry.rs`, and the decision file `docs/decisions/3843-start-side-arc.md` lists the named-entry case.\n",
